  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the author of the OG Web themes (LOT-193), I need the forum's own stylesheets captured and committed, so that every colour of those themes is traced to HFR and not guessed.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Logged out, one GET each: the stylesheet the forum serves for the default skin and for the grey skin (`/include/the_style1.php` with each skin's parameter, as the forum pages link it: read the `<link>` of a captured page first) and the static `the_style.css`; the logo `/img/forum_logo.gif` (for `orange-hfr`, the colour of the logo square and « .FR »).\n- Commit them as fixtures per [docs/FIXTURES.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/FIXTURES.md) (no cookie, no pseudo: a stylesheet has none, check anyway) with the capture date and URLs; record in `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` which URL serves which skin.\n- A 2026-10-28 agent session fetched these once into a local folder outside the repository; it is not a source (AGENTS §3): capture again.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Files committed under the fixtures tree with their URL and date; gitleaks green.\n- [ ] HFR-PROTOCOL.md names the URL of each skin's stylesheet and how a page selects it.\n- [ ] LOT-193's issue is told the fixture paths.\n\n### Before you start\n\nRead AGENTS.md §3, docs/FIXTURES.md, docs/agents/MAC-SESSIONS.md. Claim with `/claim <session-id>`; PR `Closes #<this issue>`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
